    <h1>Lab</h1>
    <p class="sub">Interactive models of financial operations. Some ideas are easier to understand when you can move a slider and watch the system respond.</p>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top: 36px;">
      <span class="card-title">Wire flow in 3D</span>
      <span class="card-context">Treasury &amp; Middle Office · three.js</span>
      <p>Payments climb a layered automation platform and arc to the bank towers, or drop to a manual desk and pile up. Drag straight-through processing from 0% to 99.9%, then raise the volume to ×18.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/lab/wire-flow/">Open the model →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <span class="card-title">Distribution waterfall in 3D</span>
      <span class="card-context">Private equity · Fund accounting · three.js</span>
      <p>Exit proceeds pour down four tiers into an investors tank and a manager tank. Compare European whole-fund carry with American deal-by-deal carry, and see where a clawback comes from.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/lab/waterfall/">Open the model →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <span class="card-title">Capability city</span>
      <span class="card-context">Business architecture · Private markets operations · three.js</span>
      <p>A capability map of a private markets manager drawn as a city. Height is operational volume and colour is automation level. Switch from today to a target state and see which capabilities become automated or agent-ready.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/lab/capability-city/">Open the model →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <span class="card-title">Career graph</span>
      <span class="card-context">2005 to today · Employers, domains, systems, results · three.js</span>
      <p>Twenty-one years of work as one connected graph. Employers rise along a spiral through time, with the domains, systems and measurable results of each around them. Take the tour or select any node.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/lab/career-graph/">Open the model →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <span class="card-title">Pipeline race</span>
      <span class="card-context">Data engineering · Row-at-a-time vs columnar · three.js</span>
      <p>Two pipelines run the same six steps on the same table. One carries each record on its own and stages every result. The other reads only the columns it needs and moves them as whole batches across several cores. Switch each advantage off to see what it contributes.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/lab/pipeline-race/">Open the model →</a>
    </div>
